#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# and

#% text
# `and(a, b, ...)`, written `a and b`, is the logical conjunction, evaluated left to right and stopping at the first `false`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# Terms that cannot be decided stay; the result is simplified as far as the known values allow.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
true and false
#% output
#= false

#% cell
1 < 2 and 3 < 4
#% output
#= true

#% cell
x > 0 and true
#% output
#= x > 0

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Conditions for `reduce` and `assuming`:

#% cell
reduce(x > 0 and x < 3 and x != 1, x, reals)
#% output
#= 0 < x and x < 1 or 1 < x and x < 3

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `or`, `not`, `every`
